    "result_text": "Build succeeds and the test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `bulkSignupWarning` flag on the owner response.\n\n**What the change does:** when more than 80 owners already carry a given (business-day-adjusted) registration date, the owner responses report `bulkSignupWarning: true`; otherwise `false`.\n\n**Files changed:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains `get/setBulkSignupWarning`.\n\n2. **`.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**:\n   - Added a `bulkSignupWarning(LocalDate)` helper that counts owners sharing the registration date and returns `count > 80` \u2014 mirroring the existing `rejectDailyLimitExceeded` accumulation path. A `null` date (e.g. seed owners) is never a warning day, guarding against NPE.\n   - Set the flag on the DTO in both `addOwner` (using the effective registration date) and `getOwner` (using the stored owner's registration date), so create and read stay consistent.\n\nI chose the controller-level approach because the value is a pure response concern that depends on a live count across all owners \u2014 the same information the daily-limit rule already uses \u2014 rather than owner state derivable in the MapStruct mapper. The threshold (`> 80`) is a named constant `BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD` documented alongside the daily-limit rule.\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreNoBulkWarningUnderThreshold`) passes: a fresh single create returns `bulkSignupWarning: false`.",
